pr: r1
title: JVM: Gradle build and the runtime layer in Kotlin
branch: pr/01-gradle-kotlin-runtime

# Section R1, log lines 1..11 (11 commits). Four groups: the StorageSpec
# follow-through stays its own commit because it is the one place this PR
# depends on nqp's StorageSpec-as-enum change (survey: N2's 221cd8a03 subject,
# "StorageSpec as a value + enum tags").

= JVM: add a Gradle build for the org.raku.rakudo runtime layer
build.gradle.kts, settings and gradle.properties for the runtime layer, and
the JVM Makefile drives the runtime jar through it instead of javac, finding
the checkout's own nqp-j rather than an installed one.
# moved: d363e9c366 pulled earlier over 9a19462f9c..d4839a6711 -- it touches
# only tools/lib/NQP/Config/Rakudo.pm and tools/templates/jvm/Makefile.in,
# the Kotlin conversions touch only src/vm/jvm/runtime/org/raku/rakudo/*.
- 6a1691243d JVM: add a Gradle build for the org.raku.rakudo runtime layer
- d363e9c366 JVM: drive the runtime jar via Gradle and find the checkout's nqp-j

= JVM: convert the runtime layer to Kotlin; container atomics on VarHandle
Binder, RakOps, RakudoContainerSpec, RakudoContainerConfigurer and
RakudoJavaInterop become Kotlin. RakudoContainerSpec's atomics move from
Unsafe to VarHandle on the way.
- 9a19462f9c JVM: convert Binder to Kotlin
- 1af327a0b8 JVM: convert RakOps to Kotlin
- c89a2ce4d3 JVM: port RakudoContainerSpec atomics from Unsafe to VarHandle
- ceb4c4657f JVM: convert RakudoContainerSpec and RakudoContainerConfigurer to Kotlin
- d4839a6711 JVM: convert RakudoJavaInterop to Kotlin

= JVM runners: overridable nqp heap, in-tree nqp home, native access
The nqp compile heap is J_NQP_MAXHEAP (default 14G; the RakuAST-era
BOOTSTRAP no longer fits 8G). The dev runner falls back to the in-tree
Gradle nqp home, enables native access, and passes nqp.library.path on as
jna.library.path.
- c960c9c8b5 JVM: make the nqp compile heap overridable, default 14G
- 2dd9fb66b5 JVM dev runner: fall back to in-tree Gradle nqp home
- 6ff32bd3c5 JVM runner: native access, and nqp.library.path for jna.library.path

= keep
- d6d6fe7bb8 JVM: follow NQP's StorageSpec to enums
